Work in the current working directory and complete this goal:

Act as a senior macOS accessibility, reliability, and privacy reviewer. Audit the planned native MSW status-bar app from the perspective of VoiceOver, keyboard-only use, reduced motion, color-blind status semantics, localization, crash/restart behavior, stale telemetry, notification policy, process cancellation, and credential redaction. Read the repository docs and exact msw failure/quarantine behavior. Return concrete UX rules, state-machine invariants, error/recovery patterns, and acceptance checks for a production app on macOS 26. Do not edit files, run project-wide tests, formatters, or linters.

Keep the change minimal and focused. Verify the work. Report a concise summary and every file changed.


**REQUIRED OUTPUT** — You MUST return ONLY a raw JSON object matching this schema:
{
  "$schema": "https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema",
  "type": "object",
  "properties": {
    "summary": {
      "type": "string",
      "minLength": 20
    },
    "filesChanged": {
      "type": "array",
      "items": {
        "type": "string"
      }
    }
  },
  "required": [
    "summary",
    "filesChanged"
  ],
  "additionalProperties": false
}
Do not include prose, markdown, headings, commentary, or code fences.
The first character of your response must be `{` and the last character must be `}`.
The workflow will fail unless the entire response is the JSON object.

